CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ cast ==: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ cast <: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ literals: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ lvalues: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ unequal: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The relational and equality operators did not dereference operands of
reference type, so `static_cast<int &>(a) == static_cast<int &>(b)'
compared the addresses of a and b.
